    "q-113047": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113047",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$23{\\text{i}}^{-1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n23{\\text{i}}^{-1}=\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the numerator and denominator by $\\text{i},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{23}{\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{i}}{\\text{i}}=\\frac{23\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{23\\text{i}}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{23\\text{i}}{(-1)}=\\frac{23}{(-1)}\\cdot \\text{i}=-23\\text{i}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
